sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant User as User
    participant QA as /qa command
    participant R as qa-researcher
    participant W as qa-writer
    participant V as qa-validator
    participant C as qa-curator
    participant FS as .claude/qa/ artifacts
    participant Jira
    participant GH as GitHub
    participant Obs as Playwright / Sentry / Datadog

    User->>QA: /qa PROJECT-123 [--quick|--standard|--exhaustive] [--force]

    rect rgb(245, 245, 235)
    Note over QA: Apply quality-engineer skill (judgement layer for all phases)
    end

    rect rgb(245, 245, 235)
    Note over QA: Step 0 - guard clauses + resume check
    QA->>FS: read existing artifacts for PROJECT-123
    FS-->>QA: surface-map / validation-report / quality-assessment (if any)
    Note over QA: Resume logic:<br/>quality-assessment exists → stop (unless --force)<br/>validation-report exists → resume from curator<br/>map COMPLETE + tests exist → resume from validator<br/>map INCOMPLETE → discard, re-run researcher<br/>map COMPLETE + no tests → resume from writer<br/>no artifacts → full pipeline
    end

    rect rgb(225, 245, 238)
    Note over R: Phase 1 - research (skipped if map already COMPLETE)
    QA->>R: invoke with ticket key
    R->>FS: read memory/<service>.md (if exists)
    FS-->>R: prior failure patterns, fragile areas
    R->>Jira: fetch ticket, AC, comments
    Jira-->>R: ticket data
    R->>GH: read diff + existing tests
    GH-->>R: code + test files
    R->>FS: write surface-map.md incrementally (Status: INCOMPLETE)
    R->>FS: mark Status: COMPLETE
    R-->>QA: map ref + AC status
    end

    QA->>User: present Test Surface Map

    alt AC missing (⚠️ NO AC FOUND)
        QA->>User: HALT - draft AC before proceeding
    else AC present
        rect rgb(225, 245, 238)
        Note over W: Phase 2 - write (skipped if test files already exist)
        QA->>W: invoke with surface map
        W->>FS: read surface-map.md
        FS-->>W: scenarios + priorities
        W->>FS: write test files
        W-->>QA: tests + coverage summary
        end

        rect rgb(225, 245, 238)
        Note over V: Phase 3 - initial validation
        QA->>V: invoke with tests + tier
        V->>Obs: run suite + check signals
        Obs-->>V: test output + baseline/after metrics
        V->>FS: write validation-report.md (raw output attached)
        V-->>QA: PASS / FAIL / BLOCKED
        end

        loop max 2 correction cycles (entered only on FAIL)
            QA->>W: re-invoke with failure output
            W->>FS: update test files
            W-->>QA: revised tests

            rect rgb(225, 245, 238)
            Note over V: Phase 3 - re-validate
            QA->>V: invoke with revised tests + tier
            V->>Obs: run suite + check signals
            Obs-->>V: test output + baseline/after metrics
            V->>FS: update validation-report.md
            V-->>QA: PASS / FAIL / BLOCKED
            end

            alt PASS or BLOCKED
                Note over QA: exit loop
            end
        end

        alt BLOCKED
            QA->>User: HALT - environment/framework issue, see validation report

        else PASS
            QA->>FS: compile quality-assessment.md

            opt tier != --quick
                rect rgb(225, 245, 238)
                Note over C: Phase 4 - curate
                QA->>C: invoke with all 3 artifacts
                C->>FS: update memory/<service>.md
                C-->>QA: curation summary
                end

                opt Jira MCP connected
                    QA->>Jira: post Quality Assessment as comment
                    Jira-->>QA: comment URL
                end
            end

            QA->>User: success - artifacts + Jira link (if posted)

        else FAIL after 2 correction cycles
            QA->>User: HALT - escalate with full validation report
        end
    end